Patch 0080: one copy of the GIF data on the game thread (GifArbiter::submitNow).
What: GifArbiter::submit copies every packet into a queue vector and the host GS thread's ring copies it again. submitNow()
is submit() + drain() for the immediately-drained case: with a host GS and an empty queue the packet is scanned
(GifHostScanner::feed, CSR SIGNAL/FINISH/LABEL, same bytes, same order) and handed to the host straight from the caller's
memory; the host copies it into the GS ring before the call returns. With a non-empty queue or no host GS it is exactly
submit() + drain(). Switched to it: PS2Memory::submitGifPacket (drainImmediately), flushMaskedPath3Packets (only when
drainImmediately and the queue is empty at entry), GS::writeRegister (host path), the VIF1 path-3 mask release (before the
fifo entry shrinks). Queued submits (not drained at once) keep their copy: their source can change before the drain.
Verified: perf_fight.py (4-player fight, blanks 6000-7800) with DON_GS_THREAD=1 built with this patch: state hash
a71d52ac6fe9b90e639d4e7d33808bbd6ecd50e0d1c28f1c8e67fac6b07906e5, equal to the reference; the linux-dev build passes.
Original work, GPL-3.0.
